CHAPTER VIII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 36
(1) The community can participate in assisting prevention efforts and handling of victims of gender-based violence and children.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of: a. providing information and or reporting any violence that comes to their knowledge;
b. providing protection for victims;
c. providing emergency assistance;T 17
d. providing advocacy to victims and or the community regarding the handling of gender-based violence and children;
e. assisting in the process of submitting applications for protection orders; f. assisting in the repatriation and social reintegration process.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, social community institutions, non-governmental organizations, educational institutions, religious institutions, private sector, and mass media.

