b. providing protection by providing complaint services, health services, social rehabilitation services, legal assistance and enforcement services, repatriation and social reintegration services, seeking to increase community participation, as well as monitoring and reporting;
c. encouraging and increasing community participation; d. cooperating with service providers in efforts to prevent, protect and recover victims of violence. (2) To carry out the obligations as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government has the authority to:
a. formulate policies and programs on the elimination of gender-based and child violence;
b. establish an integrated service center;
c. establish complaint service institutions at the sub-district level; T
d. facilitate the implementation of integrated service centers and activities of complaint service institutions at the sub-district level; e. provide facilities and infrastructure;
f. increase the capacity of service provider institutions;
g. coordinate and cooperate in the implementation of protection for victims of gender-based and child violence; h. encourage and increase community participation; i. conduct monitoring and evaluation.
(3) In the implementation of its obligations, responsibilities and authorities, the Regent may delegate to related SKPD.
(4) Related SKPD that receive delegation from the Regent as referred to in paragraph (3) shall in its implementation prepare a Regional Action Plan for the protection of victims.

Article 9
Neglect as referred to in Article 5 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of a child properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts that neglect a person within the household scope; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting decent work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

